  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: libserial\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 063142d6bfe08898316e9a6055f2ddeedef56de06f7cfc8dcdfecc6efabf4bdd\n  patches:\n    # Backport making docs/tests/examples/python components optional in CMake;\n    # see https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial/pull/133 and\n    # https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial/pull/196\n    - patches/0001-make-optional-components-configurable.patch\n    # Backport of https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial/pull/186:\n    # add missing <cstdint> include for uint8_t (needed with modern compilers)\n    - patches/0002-include-cstdint-for-uint8_t.patch\n    # Backport Linux-specific encapsulation to support macOS\n    - patches/0003-add-linux-specific-encapsulation-for-macos.patch\n    # Wrap Linux-only baud rate switch cases in SerialPort.cpp with #ifdef __linux__\n    # to match the existing guards in SerialPortConstants.h (needed for macOS);\n    # backport of https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial/pull/128\n    - patches/0004-wrap-linux-baudrates-with-ifdef.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  # See https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial/issues/140\n  skip:\n    - win\n  script:\n    - build.sh\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n  run_exports:\n    # There is no strict upstream documentation on this, so we are conservative here\n    # (the project never did a patch release, so x.x is a good compromise)\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('libserial', upper_bound='x.x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      include:\n        - libserial/SerialPort.h\n      lib:\n        - serial\n  - script:\n      - pkg-config --exists libserial\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - pkg-config\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial\n  repository: https://github.com/crayzeewulf/libserial\n  summary: Serial port programming library for C++\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE.txt\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - traversaro\n",
